@sagirem  rebar, or "resizable BAR" basically allows the GPU to negotiate the "bar size" (bar means "base address register). 

For example, modern game assets are getting larger and larger, and what reBAR does is allows those large assets to be sent in full. 

Basically, it's very technical and I still don't have a good grasp on it, but you don't need to know what it is in order to understand it's performance impact. It is intriguing to dig into it though.

